const HTML=`<p>The cell is full. Not occupied; <em>full</em>. Kuo-toa are packed in shoulder to wet shoulder, so tightly that some of them cannot sit down, standing with their bulging eyes pressed to the bars and their mouths working at the air. The floor is slick. The smell is a low-tide smell, a long way from any tide.</p>
<p>They don't fight each other for room. They seem past that. One of them is still mending a net that isn't there, fingers knotting nothing, over and over.</p>
<p>It would have been simpler to kill them. The drow are not a people who do things the hard way out of mercy. Whoever put them here wanted them alive, for something, and didn't much care in what condition.</p>
<section class="secret">
<p><strong>GM:</strong> A <strong>booking error</strong>. They were meant for the Spider Kennels, as live feed for the House watch-spiders, and should be in the beast pens with the other stock. The intake clerk logged them as prisoners ("net-menders, one lot") and nobody has been willing to sign the paperwork to move them, so they sit here until someone notices or they die.</p>
