<p>The barman of the <strong>Cooling Trough</strong>, the tavern on the canal street of the Molten Ward. A big, slow, soot-grey man behind an L-shaped bar, four stools along it, barrels stacked through the doorway to the west. He pours carefully, wipes the same cup longer than it needs, and watches the door.</p>
<p>The bar runs on a House licence, and most of the people drinking at it wear House colours.</p>
<section class="secret">
<h3>GM — Glenmill</h3>
<p><strong>Who he is.</strong> Human, surface-born freedman, about fifty. Taken as a boy from a surface town called Glenmill; he kept the town's name because the drow never asked for his own. Thirty years a kitchen thrall in the Drow Prison, bought free by cooking for the right sergeant, now runs House Barrabin's own tavern on a Barrabin licence. The only human face the party will see tonight, and he owes everything to the people hunting them.</p>
<p><strong>Block.</strong> MM 2024 Tough (CR ½, 100 XP). Mace reskinned as a cudgel (same numbers); heavy crossbow removed. Neutral, linked, green ring. Never fights: he gets under the bar.</p>
<p><strong>Personality / wants.</strong> Slow, careful, kind in the way of someone who cannot afford to be. Wants his licence renewed at the next dimming and never to be a thrall again. Wants news of the surface more than he will admit.</p>
<p><strong>Opening.</strong> He knows what they are at a glance (sunskins, prison-thin, no escort) and does not say so. Pours three cups: <em>"On the House. Drink it slow and go out the way you came — the Watch is at the end of my bar."</em> (That is the on-duty detail, group 3: Rhyzaen, Nyzeth, Shivaen.)</p>
<p><strong>What he accepts.</strong> A true story about any surface town buys him — <strong>DC 10 Persuasion</strong>, advantage if a PC names a real place. Caven and Marrith both can.</p>
<p><strong>What he can do.</strong> Hide them in the cellar (barrel room west of the bar) for one dimming, if the detail has not seen them. Tell them the Trough's back door opens on the canal street and that "the fire-keepers' tunnels" run under the canal wall — he has seen the keepers go down.</p>
<p><strong>What he will not do.</strong> Lie to a priestess: if Shivaen asks him directly, he tells her. Fight: never.</p>
<p><strong>Fear.</strong> His manumission is Barrabin's and revocable. If the party is recaptured and he helped, he goes back to the kitchens — he knows it, and it is why he hesitates.</p>
</section>`;
