const bio=`<p>A slight drow man in a good dark coat, sitting very straight behind a desk in a small locked room off the street: ledger open, quill wet, a loose heap of gold at his elbow and a red embroidered rug under his chair. Barrels against the walls. He writes in a small, even hand and does not look up until he has finished the line.</p>
<p>Precise, polite, and never surprised. He talks about everything as a price.</p>
<section class="secret">
<p><strong>GM — Ketharis "the Ledger"</strong> (KETH-ah-ris). Houseless drow, licensed pawnbroker and passes-writer. Noble (MM 2024), CR 1/8, 9 HP; rapier kept, a thin one, under the desk. Linked, Neutral. Sitting. <strong>The door is locked:</strong> DC 13 Thieves' Tools, or knock.</p>
<p><strong>Why he matters.</strong> The party has nothing and needs coin, papers and a buyer. He is all three, for a price that is always too high.</p>
<p><strong>Wants:</strong> profit; his licence (Barrabin's) renewed. <strong>Fears:</strong> Barrabin finding out what he writes for other Houses.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Buys anything</strong> at a tenth of its worth, no questions. Would pay properly for Caven's Ring of Spell Storing or a Pearl of Power if they ever get them back. For <strong>Nalveth's Registrar's Seal</strong> (if looted from the prison) he trades a great deal: a transit chit <em>and</em> 50 gp <em>and</em> a name at the Hearth (Borgra).</li>
<li><strong>Sells a transit chit</strong>: a House-errand pass good for one patrol stop (passes Rhyzaen at DC 12, group 3). Price 25 gp, or a favour: "Three sunskins are worth something to House Ilphrin tonight. Let me be the one who sold you to them." <strong>DC 13 Persuasion</strong> gets the chit on credit against the Ilphrin sale.</li>
<li><strong>Lies:</strong> he accepts none and needs none; he does not have to believe them, only to profit.</li>
<li><strong>Will not:</strong> fight (he hides under the desk and screams), or be seen helping them while a priestess is in the street.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>The sealed letter</strong> on the desk is a settlement note in trade-cant for the <strong>Grey Road caravan</strong>: "Grey Road, one lot, people included, received in full, for the Merrowgate paper." He brokered the handover Thrund Grimtongue arranged. Tomas and Edda Brell were sold, not ambushed; the party can read it off his desk.</p>
<p><strong>Loot:</strong> the coin heap is 60 gp. Barrabin's licence-mark is stamped on the ledger's spine, which is the leverage he fears: threaten to show it to the House and he gives.</p>
</section>`;
