<section class="secret"><h2>GM</h2>
<p><strong>Who she is.</strong> Svirfneblin, bond-cook to the House Barrabin barracks under a House licence — indentured, not enslaved: there is a paper and a term. Four years left; the notches on the counter edge are the years. A deep gnome in a drow kitchen is a trophy and a convenience at once. Commoner (CR 0, 10 XP). Not a fight. Neutral.</p>
<p><strong>Wants.</strong> Her bond paid down; her kitchen-boy <strong>Skritch</strong> back (the kobold now in the prison kitchen, requisitioned from her last season); the three men at her oven-back gone before they crack her flue.</p>
<p><strong>Fears.</strong> The Veiled Sons crew behind her oven. The Watch finding sunskins at her counter (her bond is revocable).</p>
<p><strong>Feeds them first.</strong> Three starving sunskins get fish-stew unasked (Caven's "Starved" tell is why). Then she asks what it is worth — anything true about the surface (she has never seen it) is enough.</p>
<p><strong>The oven vent (group 8).</strong> She hears the crew through the flue and has understood about a third of it. <strong>DC 10 Persuasion</strong> (free if anyone names Skritch): "There is a flask in my vent and a House man in my lane, and the one with the voice said <em>Hollow Moon</em> twice. I do not know what that is. I do know they will kill me if they think I heard." Cheapest route to the group-8 secret; it puts her life in the party's hands.</p>
<p><strong>The back door.</strong> Opens on the oven-back corner — the crew's exit. She can bar it from inside, trapping their retreat, but only if the party promises to take her with them or to get Skritch out.</p>
<p><strong>The bond paper</strong> is in the cheese crock. Burn it and she is free by drow law — no paper, no bond — and she knows it.</p>
</section>`;
