<p><strong>What the room is.</strong> The founder's hearth: Kharg the Fiery, a duergar fire-smith, cut the lava channels; the drow took the city; the channels still need his keepers. The priesthood licenses it as a <em>guild hearth</em> — never a temple — and a priestess sits in the spider chair one dimming in ten. The red-ribboned scroll is that licence. The pressed red flowers are fire-poppy, the Hearth's offering. The big statue-hall in the south-west is the ward's real Lolth chapel.</p>
<p><strong>The meeting.</strong> House Ilphrin (Saelzir in the dispensary below, Vexaen at the west door) is buying one night's use of the keepers' cooling tunnels under the canal walls — out of the ward under the gate chain — for "goods not named". The herbalist carries the paper up and down; drow do not say terms aloud. The Hearth has sold tunnel-nights before, never to a House at war with the House that holds its licence (Barrabin). She is pricing the risk and is slow on purpose.</p>
