 { marker:"jt498EQYKGgyxOXH", folder:fC, uuid:"Compendium.dnd-monster-manual.actors.Actor.mmSpy00000000000", name:"Zelvra", art:T+"shadar-kai/shadar-kai-observant.png", ring:RS+"shadar-kai-observant-373b9c.webp", dv:120, sub:"Elf (drow)", size:"med", attrs:["housebarrabin","nathryldhaun"], conceal:{housebarrabin:3},
   bio:`<p><strong>Zelvra</strong> (ZEL-vrah), a drow woman in a plain dark coat, hood up, sitting with her back to the bar at the corner table. Two copies of a paper lie between her and the dwarf opposite, with a stick of grey wax and a small seal. She writes quickly and stops whenever someone at the bar laughs.</p><section class="secret"><h3>GM — Zelvra, lesser purse-steward of House Barrabin</h3><p>MM Spy, CR 1 (200 XP). Shortsword kept as a stiletto; hand crossbow with drow poison (DC 13 CON or poisoned 1 hour; fail by 5+ unconscious). Drow overlay incl. <em>Faerie Fire</em> and <em>Darkness</em> 1/day. Linked, green ring, Neutral. House Barrabin is DC 13 on her (conceal +3): sigil turned inward, no House colours.</p><p><strong>The contract.</strong> Barrabin's purse is empty (the House's weakness lore) and the cell-block payroll is due at the next dimming. Zelvra is borrowing from the Garhammar Trade League, through Dugbor: forty crossbows, bolts and six months' wages for the prison guard. It is secured against <em>"the labour of the lower cells, the next three lots"</em>, to be hired out to League mines. The pledge list includes <strong>"three sunskins, lower cells"</strong>, which is the party. She signs with her own steward's seal, not the Matron's. Nobody above her knows. If the guard goes unpaid the Watch walks, and she would rather be hanged for this than for that.</p><p><strong>Why the corner.</strong> It is the Trough's <em>blind table</em>, older than Glenmill: the barman never serves it, nobody at the bar turns to look, and whatever is signed there "was never said in a House's house". A pledge witnessed in a House tavern goes in the House book, which the Matron's daughters read. A pledge of souls owes the priesthood its tenth, and there is a novice priestess at the end of the bar (Shivaen). The canal window behind the table hisses with lava and covers voices. She sits with her back to the bar so nobody reads her face.</p><p><strong>Wants:</strong> the seal on the paper and to be gone before Shivaen looks round. <strong>Fears:</strong> the House book; Vaelith; the priesthood's tenth.</p><p><strong>If she sees the party:</strong> panic, hidden. Three of her collateral are loose, and she cannot call the Watch over without the Watch seeing the paper. She will want them quietly recaptured and does nothing loud.</p><p><strong>The lever.</strong> The contract proves the Barrabin purse is empty and a steward is pledging without the Matron's seal. Saelzir (Ilphrin) would pay well for it. Borgra counts it as "proof they hold Barrabin's secrets". Held over Zelvra with the paper in hand (<strong>DC 14 Intimidation or Persuasion</strong>), she writes them a steward's transfer chit: "prisoners in transfer, steward's authority". It passes any Barrabin checkpoint (Rhyzaen, the gate guards) without a roll.</p><p><strong>If it goes wrong:</strong> she holds the contract to the table lamp, burns it, and slips toward the canal door. She fights only if cornered.</p></section>`+DROW,
