const bio=`<p>A thin, grey-skinned man in a tallow-stained apron, standing at the corner of the lane under the canal wall with a crate of tallow blocks at his feet. Cropped white hair, a drow's ears, a jaw that is not a drow's. Through the open door behind him is a narrow stone-floored shop: tall racks of dipped candles hung by their wicks along the far wall, and a worktable at the back with a tally-book, a quill and a pot of ink.</p><p>He has the easy, careful pleasantness of a man who sells light to everyone in the street and has never once been on the wrong side of any of them. He is waiting for someone, and it is not you.</p>
<section class="secret"><h2>GM</h2>
<p><strong>Who he is.</strong> Orrin (OR-in), tallow-chandler, half-drow, 30s, Molten Ward born. Commoner (CR 0, 10 XP) — not a fight; if hit he drops the pole and runs inside. Darkvision 60. Neutral. Joe has not decided what he is: he is a bystander who could go any way, and the branches below are written as <em>triggers</em>, not outcomes.</p>
<p><strong>Why a chandler.</strong> Everyone in the ward buys light from him — the chapel its altar candles, the Hearth its tallow, the barracks its lamps, the Trough its tapers. He knows everyone's door and owes everyone a little. He is also the cheapest light on the map for a party that has none.</p>
<p><strong>Tonight.</strong> He is waiting in the lane for <strong>Kelzaer</strong> (group R2-3, Barrabin's Steward of Licences) to come past, because his tallow licence is re-stamped by the same hand tonight. His stamp is his licence is his shop.</p>
<p><strong>Wants.</strong> His stamp, his evening, and nothing to happen near his shop. <strong>Fears.</strong> Being seen on the wrong side of whoever is in the street; losing the licence. He has no opinion about sunskins yet — that is the point.</p>
<h3>The branches</h3>
<p><strong>Helps</strong> — <em>when</em> they buy (even on a promise against "the sunskins' gear in the Keeper's chest" — he has heard of it), or anyone is simply kind to him, <em>and</em> nobody from the inspection party (R2-3) is looking. <em>Then:</em> sells a bundle of six candles and a shuttered tin lantern; tells them the chapel door is "the Seat's tonight, not yours"; tells them the Trough's back door opens on the canal street; and offers to walk them <strong>past the inspection party as his carriers</strong>, a tallow-bundle each on the shoulder — his lie, their faces: <strong>DC 11 Deception</strong> (group check), advantage if they are actually carrying his crate.</p>
<p><strong>Ignores</strong> — <em>when</em> they walk past, haggle and buy nothing, or ask him nothing. <em>Then:</em> keeps dipping. Says nothing to anyone, because saying things costs. If Kelzaer asks later: "three sunskins, going west" — true and useless.</p>
<p><strong>Sells them out</strong> — <em>when</em> they threaten him, take anything, Nedylene (the priestess, R2-3) sees him with them, or Kelzaer asks him a direct question while the party is still in sight. <em>Then:</em> tells Kelzaer everything he saw, at once, as the price of his stamp — and points. Not malice: the stamp is the shop.</p>
<p><strong>Undecided</strong> — nothing above has happened by the time it matters. Roll <strong>d6: 1–2 helps, 3–4 ignores, 5–6 sells.</strong> He is a bystander; the die is honest.</p>
<h3>The lever</h3>
<p>His father is <strong>Rhyzaen</strong> (round 1, group 3 — the House-born lieutenant at the bar), who does not know and would not care. Orrin knows. A PC who says that name in front of him gets a flinch; gentle about it → the <strong>help</strong> branch for free; not gentle → the <strong>sell</strong> branch. It is the one thing in the ward he cares about more than the stamp.</p>
<p><strong>Social DCs.</strong> Persuasion DC 10 to get directions or a sale on credit; Intimidation works (DC 8) but always triggers the sell branch the moment the party is out of sight. Insight DC 12 reads him (see the tells).</p>
</section>`;
