const specs=[
{key:"L7lw", name:"Nedylene", block:"mmPriest00000000", art:"drow-with-magic-pipe", rs:"drow-with-magic-pipe-f089a0.webp", ring:GREEN, linked:true,
 overlay:["Fey Ancestry","Sunlight Sensitivity","Drow Magic"], langs:["elvish","undercommon"], attrs:["housebarrabin","nathryldhaun"],
 items:(it)=>{ if(it.name==="Radiant Flame"){it.name="Spider's Bite";setTypes(it,"radiant","necrotic");}
   if(it.name==="Mace"){it.name="Snake-headed Rod";setTypes(it,"radiant","necrotic");} },
 bio:`<p><strong>Nedylene</strong>. A drow priestess in a dark, spider-worked robe, an ember-pipe lit between two fingers and a snake-headed rod across her lap. She is in no hurry, and she makes sure the street can see it.</p>
<p><em>Says:</em> "Is it ten minutes yet?" / (to the steward) "Count faster." / (to a sunskin) "And what are <em>you</em> for?"</p>
${S(`<p><strong>GM.</strong> Priestess of the Seat, a Barrabin cousin (not of the line). MM 2024 <strong>Priest</strong>, CR 2 (450 XP). Reskin: Radiant Flame → <em>Spider's Bite</em> (necrotic, same dice); mace → snake-headed rod (its extra damage necrotic); Spirit Guardians reads as spectral spiders. Drow overlay: Darkvision 120, Fey Ancestry, Sunlight Sensitivity, Darkness and Faerie Fire 1/day.</p>
<p><strong>The inspection.</strong> The Witness-chapel's licence is re-stamped once a year by the Seat with House Barrabin co-signing. Tonight. She is here to be seen; Kelzaer has the stamp. The inspection goes in through the chapel's north door <strong>ten minutes of real play</strong> after the party arrives on the map. If the party is inside without a Register entry when the door opens, Bramblepin answers the first question honestly.</p>
<p><strong>Wants:</strong> to be gone, to the Seat before the Feast. Secretly, a reason to revoke the chapel's licence; a surface chapel in a Barrabin ward is an embarrassment she was sent to tolerate. <strong>Fears:</strong> nothing on this map; a senior priestess hearing she was <em>useful</em> to sunskins. She will not act on a sunskin's word without something she can show.</p>
<p><strong>The dark lever.</strong> A PC who hands her an irregularity ("the Prior hides people", "the dwarf has a grate key") gets her delighted attention and a <strong>pass through the ward under her name</strong>: a word to any post, the Chain Gate included. It costs four clerics their freedom. Cheapest way out on the map; let them feel the price. Drogmok-dur, if alive, will remember.</p>
<p>"Ilphrin's purchase" makes her look up: wrong answer, interesting answer. She sends Tazrin to the Hearth to ask; the party has the length of his walk.</p>
<p><strong>If it goes wrong:</strong> <em>Bless</em>, then <em>Spirit Guardians</em>, and walks at the softest PC. Capture over kill: "alive, worth money". If she drops, Tazrin surrenders.</p>`)}`,
 lore:[tell("The pipe","prc",10,"An ember-pipe, lit, on a House errand. Nobody has told her to hurry and nobody will."),
   tell("Who she hates","ins",12,"She looks at the chapel door the way you would look at a stain. She has been sent to tolerate it."),
   tell("Not the one with the stamp","ins",12,"She outranks everyone in the street, and she is not the one doing the work. Whatever is being decided tonight, the nervous one with the slate is deciding it."),
   tell("Cousin, not daughter","his",14,"The sigil on the rod is the House's, but the rod is plain. A cousin of the House, not of the line, sent because somebody had to be.")]},
{key:"92SF", name:"Kelzaer", block:"mmMageApprentice", art:"drow-caster", rs:"drow-caster-4fed29.webp", ring:GREEN, linked:true,
 overlay:["Fey Ancestry","Sunlight Sensitivity","Drow Magic"], langs:["common","elvish","undercommon"], attrs:["housebarrabin","nathryldhaun"],
 items:(it)=>{ if(it.name==="Ice Knife"){it.name="Web-shard";} },
 bio:`<p><strong>Kelzaer</strong>. A drow male in a steward's dark coat, a slate of tallies under one arm and a seal-ring on a cord around his neck. His lips move while he reads. He is counting something, and he keeps glancing at the priestess to see if she has noticed how long it is taking.</p>
<p><em>Says:</em> "Whose paper?" / "Forty-one, forty-two..." / (to the priestess) "Nearly, Mistress."</p>
${S(`<p><strong>GM.</strong> House Barrabin's Steward of Licences. MM 2024 <strong>Mage Apprentice</strong>, CR 2 (450 XP). Reskin: Ice Knife → <em>Web-shard</em> (piercing + cold, same dice); Disguise Self kept. Drow overlay: Darkvision 120, Fey Ancestry, Sunlight Sensitivity, Darkness and Faerie Fire 1/day. Speaks Common (he deals with the chapel).</p>
<p><strong>Rank:</strong> the priestess outranks him, he outranks the clerk, the blade reports to him and obeys her. But tonight <em>he</em> matters: he has the stamp. Insight 12 on the group shows it; players who see it skip the priestess.</p>
<p><strong>"Whose paper?"</strong> Here, three sunskins walking up to a surface chapel are what the street expects. "Merrowgate's" passes at <strong>DC 10 Deception</strong> (advantage if a Witness in earshot nods; <strong>no roll</strong> if Edrow has already entered them in the Register, because Kelzaer reads it). "Ilphrin's purchase" makes him blink and Nedylene look up.</p>
<p><strong>The bribe.</strong> He will "not count you" for anything with a House value. The party has nothing, but a promise against "the sunskins' gear in the Keeper's chest" is a thing he has heard of and wants (<strong>DC 13 Persuasion</strong>). Never where she can see; a PC has to get him three steps up the lane.</p>
<p><strong>Wants:</strong> the tally to balance, and a gift "for the House" that stays in his sleeve. <strong>Fears:</strong> her seeing him take it. Orrin the chandler is waiting in the lane for his stamp too; if Kelzaer asks him a direct question while the party is in sight, Orrin talks.</p>
<p><strong>If it goes wrong:</strong> <em>Thunderwave</em> to open the lane and <strong>runs north for the Chain Gate</strong>: that is the alarm, forty seconds of running. He never comes back.</p>`)}`,
 lore:[tell("The stamp","inv",11,"A seal-ring on a cord, not a finger. It comes off to be used, and it is the only thing about him that is not nervous."),
   tell("What he is counting","ins",12,"He is rehearsing numbers. Somebody is about to be counted and he has to get it right."),
   tell("A sleeve with room in it","ins",14,"He looks at your hands before your faces, then at the priestess, then away. He could be bought, but not where she can see it.")]},
{key:"1Xnc", name:"Dinzael", block:"mmCommoner000000", art:"drow-determined", rs:"drow-determined-a2b842.webp", ring:GREEN, linked:true,
 overlay:["Fey Ancestry","Sunlight Sensitivity"], langs:["common","elvish","undercommon"], attrs:["nathryldhaun"],
 items:(it)=>{ if(it.name==="Club"){it.name="Seal-box";it.system.description.value=`<p>[[/attack extended]]. [[/damage average extended]].</p><p>A flat iron box on a strap. It is a weapon only if he throws it, and he would rather not.</p>`;} },
 extra:[{name:"House Licence Seal",type:"loot",img:"icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",system:{quantity:1,description:{value:"<p>A House seal and a cake of black wax in a felt-lined iron box: the mark that stamps a licence in this ward. Pressed on a chit, it reads as the House's own.</p>"}}},
        {name:"Stamped Blank Chit",type:"loot",img:"icons/sundries/documents/document-symbol-eye.webp",system:{quantity:3,description:{value:"<p>A House chit, already sealed in black wax, with the lines for name and purpose left empty.</p>"}}}],
 bio:`<p><strong>Dinzael</strong>. A young drow in plain dark clothes, sorting papers on the lid of a flat iron box that hangs from a strap at his shoulder. He has the gift of being nobody in particular.</p>
<p><em>Says:</em> almost nothing. "Yes, Steward." / "It is in the box, Steward."</p>
${S(`<p><strong>GM.</strong> The inspection's clerk, 20. MM 2024 <strong>Commoner</strong>, CR 0 (10 XP). Club → seal-box (1d4, a weapon only if thrown). Darkvision 120, Fey Ancestry, Sunlight Sensitivity. No House blood; carries the ward, not the House.</p>
<p><strong>The seal-box</strong> holds <strong>Barrabin's licence seal</strong>, which forges a House stamp the way Nalveth's Registrar's Seal does, and <strong>three stamped blank chits</strong>: each passes any post at the Ketharis chit's DCs (the Chain Gate at DC 12). The second forging tool on the map. On the sheet as loot.</p>
<p><strong>Wants:</strong> not to be noticed. <strong>Fears:</strong> both of them. A kind word and no witnesses could get a chit out of him (DC 15 Persuasion, or DC 13 Intimidation where the steward cannot see; he gives it and then forgets you were ever there).</p>
<p><strong>If it goes wrong:</strong> gets behind the crate with the seal-box and keeps it.</p>`)}`,
 lore:[tell("The box","prc",11,"A flat iron box on a strap, kept under the arm. Papers, ink, and something that clinks: a seal and its wax."),
   tell("Nobody","ins",10,"He has made himself the least interesting person in the street, which is a skill."),
   tell("Afraid of both of them","ins",13,"He flinches a fraction when either of the other two speaks. Whatever happens in this street, he will be the one blamed for it.")]},
{key:"ONiY", name:"Tazrin", block:"mmWarriorVeteran", art:"drow-sellsword", rs:"drow-sellsword-156481.webp", ring:GREY, linked:false,
 overlay:["Fey Ancestry","Sunlight Sensitivity","Drow Magic"], langs:["elvish","undercommon"], attrs:["housebarrabin","nathryldhaun"],
 items:(it)=>{ if(it.name==="Greatsword"){it.name="Longsword";}
